The bottlenecks are now memory movement: the Triton gate/layout pass is ~3.6 ms and the channel-major-to-row-major output transpose is ~4.6 ms on the largest D=128 case; the BF16 batched GEMM itself is only ~1.1 ms. Next I’m testing whether PyTorch’s native transpose kernels beat my first Triton layout kernel, then I’ll decide whether a fused final kernel is worth it.
