+"""
+TriMul forward optimized around the cubic contraction.
+
+The input is layer-normalized with PyTorch, the five hidden projections are
+computed as one packed BF16 GEMM, and a Triton kernel applies sigmoid gates,
+mask, and layout conversion into channel-major [B, H, N, N] matrices.  The
+outgoing triangle contraction then becomes B*H independent N x N BF16 GEMMs via
+torch.bmm.  A second Triton kernel performs output LayerNorm and gate directly
+from the channel-major contraction before the final PyTorch output projection.
